   "heading": "HAROLD WIDOM’S WORK IN RANDOM MATRIX THEORY 1. Introduction The distributions of random matrix theory govern the statistical properties of a wide variety of large systems which do not obey the usual laws of classical probability. Such systems appear in many diﬀerent areas of applied science and tech",
